# nvn/compute: keep NDVE running after a Metal compiler death (#2920)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/9df3c09fc6f231b1baac94ecb28c6db9e2618990  (issue #2920)
# Author:    seedds, 2026-11-21 01:48:34 +0800
# Co-authors:
#   Co-authored-by: David Padron-Harris
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); the attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES FOR THE PHONE
#   Ocarina of Time (Switch 2) runs a neural up-scaling / correction chain (NDVE, 37 kernels) as guest compute dispatches. When Metal's compiler service is interrupted (upstream's case: an M2
#   MacBook Air; whether the phone's compiler service dies under its memory ceiling is NOT known, nothing in the Ocarina log says so), a compute pipeline that failed that way was latched as
#   failed ("cps_failed") for the whole session and NDVE's sequence broke (green striped blocks in the opening movie). Now (1) NDVE gets each prepared dispatch BEFORE the translated pipeline
#   is looked up, (2) an interrupted compile (err_compiler_died) is not latched: the dispatch is skipped and a later one retries, (3) permanent refusals are still cached. dispatch_pso() is
#   the old lookup / build code moved out of dispatch_. Default: on, no switch.
# Applies on top of 0455. RISK: low-medium (compute dispatch path of every game). NOT run on a device. Shader chain id untouched.
#
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0415 and the candidates numbered below this one, in the order of the numbers of this folder.

diff --git a/dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m b/dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m
